From 275b612456bceb942bc6520a22883d75ffaa412b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A place under a macro call is still a place

(ref (((G L) 'mainth) 'l)), Lua's &G(L)->mainth.l, gave the address
of a copy of mainth: node-type leaves a macro call untyped, so the
receiver ((G L) 'mainth) was emitted as a struct value and stored in
a temporary. emit-untyped-receiver takes a field receiver's address
instead; the 1-argument ref, the field ref and set!'s receiver use it.
Found by the nuc-lua port (its ISSUE-043).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
